From 3deb6fd22117a65b34cce4066a5266488a0e16a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 08:33:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media queries: range syntax and @custom-media
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two Media Queries gaps that made a query which should match not match, so a
document rendered as if the rules inside it did not exist.

**Range syntax (Media Queries 4 §2.4).** `(width > 0px)` did not parse: the
condition was split on `:` only, so the whole thing read as one feature name,
failed the <ident> test and evaluated as <general-enclosed> — false, and false
under `not` too. All three forms are handled now — `<name> <op> <value>`,
`<value> <op> <name>` (which asserts the same thing with the comparison
flipped) and the two-sided `<value> <lt> <name> <lt> <value>` — over every
feature the evaluator already knew, not just width.

The strict comparisons are why `MediaFeatureRange` grows rather than reusing
`Min`/`Max`: `>` is not `min-`, and a viewport exactly on the bound is the case
that tells them apart. Range syntax has no prefixed spelling, so `min-width`
appearing where a feature name goes is rejected — otherwise it would silently
become the feature it prefixes. A comparison that is present but malformed
(three operators, mismatched directions, a non-ident in the name position) is
`not all`, and stays false under `not`, like every other unknown term.

**@custom-media (Media Queries 5 §3).** `@custom-media --foo (width > 0px);`
parsed into a `CssAtRule` nothing ever read. Definitions are now collected from
every registered sheet, keyed to the sheet generation so they are rebuilt
exactly when the rule index is, and `(--foo)` resolves against them. Collection
is separate from evaluation because a custom media query is document-global: a
definition *below* the `@media` rule that references it still applies to it.
`true`/`false` are honoured, an undefined name is unknown rather than false
(so `not (--undefined)` does not match either), and a definition that reaches
itself is a cycle — invalid, and guarded, since without the guard it recurses
until the stack runs out.

Exit gate: 39 new cases in CssStyleEngineTests over the range grammar (both
operand orders, both two-sided directions, non-length features, the malformed
shapes, composition with `and`/`not`) and @custom-media (resolution, definition
after use, true/false, undefined, direct and mutual cycles).
Broiler.CSS.Dom.Tests 426 passed with the 2 pre-existing CssDomArchitectureTests
failures (verified on a clean tree); Broiler.CSS.Tests 341/341.

WPT reftests: css/mediaqueries/at-custom-media-basic passes, and a 458-test
subset spanning css/mediaqueries, css/css-nesting, css/css-values and
css/css-conditional moves 301 -> 302 with no test changing the other way.

